{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449992-did-anyone-ever-make-technocratic-pillars","id":1449992,"title":"Did anyone ever make technocratic pillars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-28T09:27:40-07:00","id":1449992,"title":"Did anyone ever make technocratic pillars?","content":"Or for that matter sons if ether etc. As it stands it's hard to use the pillars in the modern age because all the printed or fan made ones have focused on mystical paradigms<br /> <br /> In particular I am at a loss to decide how much spirit Magix they should have access too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T09:33:44-07:00","id":1449994,"title":"","content":"Not Pillars, no. But if you take a look at my signature, you will find a Machine Sphere which was designed for the Sons of Ether, and an outline for Fields for the Technocracy, which is basically an alternate arrangement of Spheres with the Technocracy in mind.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy does such a wide variety of things that attempting to fit everything they do into four Pillars strikes me is sheer Madness. What I would do instead would be to give each Convention four Pillars selected out of my set of nine Fields. Given that there are five Conventions and nine Pillars, there's bound to be a lot of overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks